\title{DFBM: Denoising abundance matrices by factorizing binary masks}
\description{
A nonparametric denoising method for nonnegative abundance matrices (samples by features). Each column is dichotomized into a nested sequence of binary masks at its own quantile thresholds. The masks are factorized jointly into low-rank probability matrices by proximal gradient descent with singular value thresholding, giving each entry an estimated survival curve over the thresholds. The denoised value is the capped expectation implied by that curve, which fills in zeros and caps extreme values. New samples are denoised with the fitted factors, without refitting.
}
